      "remainingWork": ["Use the 1,909-entry revision-aligned semantic-review queue to establish canonical game-entity and activity identities from retained source signatures and contexts, then prove repeatability, membership, requirements, variants, XP, timing, mechanics, and authoritative exclusions. Begin with the 29 explicit activity-page candidates, but do not treat activity/minigame page type as repeatability proof; distinguish reference collections and composites from actual trainable method variants. Reconcile 68 queued untyped pages, 4,725 stable rendered pages without unlock evidence, 1,565 unlock pages without rendered-guide evidence, five unresolved rendered targets, the wider unlock set's 137 untyped pages and 31 activity pages, and 51 ambiguous statement forms. Historical template-expansion provenance remains open because dependency revision IDs and the generative origins of 16,284 rendered-only observations are unavailable. Continue independent discovery until every repeatable training activity in every skill is enumerated. The central guide index's composite Combat row and four Defence link disagreements remain explicit. Rockslide pairing still requires complete activity and travel graphs.", "Add or repair 9 target-level condition models. Al Kharid now has independently revision-pinned Tightrope 1 and zip-line facts, but both level-34 success probabilities, failed-attempt XP, and recovery routing/time remain unpublished; its guide rate remains scoped to levels 20–30. Penguin access is resolved to completed Cold War or the explicit in-progress course milestone, but its level-34 failure probability and applicable observed-rate scope remain unpublished. Shayzien Basic now retains its seven-obstacle route and proves that its three Tightrope occurrences cannot fail, but the failure-capable identity among Ladder, Monkeybars, Bar, and Gap, aggregate level-34 probability, failed-attempt XP, recovery route/time, and current expected rate remain unpublished; t